# The fundamental development guideline for making any changes

# Running command in terminal

This project uses Nix to manage the development environment. Run `nix develop` once in every new terminal window to start the Nix environment. For AI agents, prefix terminal commands with `nix develop -c`:

```
nix develop -c <command>
```

**Git exception:** Run `git` directly (`git status`, `git diff`, `git commit`, etc.) — no Nix prefix.

## Run Tests

Always run all tests instead of just one test file:

```bash
nix develop -c pytest          # Run all tests
nix develop -c make test       # Same via Makefile
```

## Run Tests and Format Checking

```bash
nix develop -c make lint       # pre-commit hooks (flake8, etc.)
```

## Automated Test Practices

* All code and logic need to be covered by unit tests
* Prefer end-to-end tests that exercise observable behavior (CLI output, translation results) over tests that mirror internal structure
* Use VCR cassettes in `tests/fixtures/cassettes/` for HTTP-based provider tests; do not mock code unless it is about the file system
